# Singularity 3.7 definition file for the foundation-model MLIP family: MACE-MP-0/OFF (via the
# mace codebase), Orb, UMA (via fairchem) -- inference/fine-tune only. Def-file syntax/sections:
# https://docs.sylabs.io/guides/3.7/user-guide/definition_files.html
# Build command: https://docs.sylabs.io/guides/3.7/user-guide/build_a_container.html
#
# CityUHK Burgundy facts baked into this file's design (see this project's Burgundy task brief):
# no sudo anywhere on the cluster (build elsewhere with sudo, SFTP the .sif to $HOME/scratch/),
# Singularity 3.7 at the fixed path /usr/bin/singularity on compute nodes, no outbound internet
# from a running job -- EXCEPT the deliberate gated-checkpoint fetch below, which happens only at
# job run time via the login-node-adjacent data-transfer path the cluster provides, never inside
# this image itself and never baked into it (see "no checkpoints baked in" below). Code at
# src/baselines/codebases/{mace,orb-models} and fairchem (shared with mlip-transformer.def, for
# UMA) is added as git submodules by sibling agents on other branches -- not present in this
# worktree, referenced here only by the paths they are documented to land at.

Bootstrap: docker
From: nvcr.io/nvidia/pytorch:24.08-py3
# Same base-image pin as the other 3 images, same reason -- independently pinned/isolated
# otherwise; this image's own consistency requirement is mace-torch + orb-models + fairchem-core
# all importing cleanly together (inference/fine-tune only, no training-from-scratch stack
# needed here, unlike mlip-mpnn.def's mace-torch pin which is used for from-scratch training).

%post
    set -eu

    pip install --no-cache-dir \
        numpy==1.26.4 \
        pytest==8.3.3 \
        mace-torch==0.3.9 \
        orb-models==0.4.0 \
        fairchem-core==1.2.0 \
        huggingface_hub==0.24.6

    # ---- NO checkpoints baked in, by design ----------------------------------------------------
    # MACE-OFF23 in particular ships under a non-commercial Academic Software License (Sylabs/
    # Apptainer def-file %post has no concept of license scope, so this must be enforced by
    # convention/process, not by the build tool). Fetching any gated checkpoint (MACE-OFF23 via
    # the mace codebase, or any gated HF-hosted UMA/Orb weights) at BUILD time would bake that
    # restrictively-licensed artifact into a .sif that might otherwise be shared/reused freely --
    # so this image installs only the fetching machinery (huggingface_hub, mace's own
    # foundations_models downloader), never a checkpoint file itself. Checkpoint fetching happens
    # at job RUN time (inside the sbatch script, using whatever HF_TOKEN/credentials the user's
    # own run-dir or environment supplies), writing into the run directory under /work, not into
    # this image.

    # ---- this project's own package (src/baselines) -------------------------------------------
    # Not installed here -- see mlip-legacy.def's %post comment for the full rationale.

    # ---- image digest: build-time placeholder only --------------------------------------------
    # See mlip-legacy.def's %post comment for the full timing-order explanation.
    mkdir -p /opt
    echo "UNVERIFIED-BUILD" > /opt/image_digest.txt

%environment
    export LC_ALL=C
    export PYTHONPATH=/work/src:${PYTHONPATH:-}
    export NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=all
    export CUDA_CACHE_DISABLE=0
    # HF_HOME deliberately left unset here (not /opt/*, which is inside the immutable image) --
    # the sbatch template points it at the bind-mounted run directory so any checkpoint fetched
    # at run time lands under /work, not inside -- or cached beside -- the image.

%labels
    Project EqFSA
    Family mlip-foundation
    Contains mace-torch-0.3.9 orb-models-0.4.0 fairchem-core-1.2.0 huggingface_hub-0.24.6

%help
    EqFSA baseline container: MACE-MP-0/OFF + Orb (v2/v3) + UMA, inference/fine-tune only.
    No checkpoints are baked in -- MACE-OFF23 is Academic-Software-License-gated and must be
    fetched at job run time into the run directory, never at image build time.
    Run via (never submitted automatically -- always a printed/handed-off command, per this
    project's standing rule):
        singularity exec --nv --bind <repo>:/work --bind <image>.sif.sha256:/opt/image_digest.txt:ro \
            --pwd /work <image>.sif \
            python -m baselines.adapters.tier3_foundation \
                --model {mace_mp_0,mace_off23,orb_v2,orb_v3,uma} --mode {zero_shot,fine_tune} ...
